A||||2||DR650SE||How do I check a code? ||||1||
Z||000000||DR650SE||10-26-2001||11:34 PM||||When the service engine light comes up how do i check the code.  Where can I get the device to plug into the link, or is there another way to do it?  Thanks for any info<P>------------------<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierozilla||10-27-2001||12:12 AM||||Take the black plastic cover off the cig lighter housing. On the pass side of it you'll see the little box thing (sorry). If you dont have the GM code key, then just use a paper clip (open it up) and stick it in the bottom pass side slots (2)...&lt;if you're sitting in the drivers seat, plug one end of the paper clip into far bottom right slot, and the other end of the paper clip into the one next to it.) <BR>Turn key to "on" position (but dont start the car). The check engine light will go "flash........flash flash" 3 times. Then it will flash your code(s). <BR>&lt;For example, if you have a code 32, it'll go "flash flash flash.........flash flash".&gt;<BR>It'll return to the "12" &lt;flash.......flash flash" when its finished.<p>[This message has been edited by Fierozilla (edited 10-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||DR650SE||10-27-2001||12:13 AM||||Thanks for the help||||reg||1
